<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/wilson.rs. std only. SU(2) Wilson lattice gauge theory on a torus::Torus, action S = beta sum_p (1 - a0(U_p)), U_p = U(x,mu) U(x+mu,nu) U(x+nu,mu)^dagger U(x,nu)^dagger, links indexed by Torus::link_index. Struct Lattice { torus, links: Vec<Quaternion>, beta, seed, replica, sweep } with cold and hot (Haar, sweep counter -1 stream) starts. staple(link) = sum over nu != mu of U(x+mu,nu) U(x+nu,mu)^dagger U(x,nu)^dagger + U(x+mu-nu,nu)^dagger U(x-nu,mu)^dagger U(x-nu,nu), so the local action is beta a0(U(x,mu) staple). One sweep = for each direction mu, for each parity of the site coordinate sum, update all those links in parallel (they share no plaquette when every side length is even; return an error from new if any side is odd) with std::thread::scope over chunks; each link update uses the stream Stream::new(seed, sweep, link index, replica), so results do not depend on the thread count. heat_bath_sweep, overrelax_sweep, and a combined update (one heat bath then n_or over-relaxation sweeps). Observables: plaquette average; rectangular Wilson loops W(R,T) averaged over all positions and planes (mu,nu) with mu < nu, both orientations; wilson_loop_table(rmax) giving all W(r,t), r,t <= rmax, from precomputed straight-line products, threaded over fixed-size site chunks summed in chunk order (independent of thread count); Creutz ratio chi(R,T) = -ln(W(R,T) W(R-1,T-1) / (W(R,T-1) W(R-1,T))). Independent tests: tests/wilson_2d.rs (2D plaquette against character::torus_plaquette at several beta, within 5 jackknife errors; result independent of thread count bit for bit; broken heat bath fails), tests/wilson_4d.rs (gauge invariance of observables under a random gauge transformation to 1e-12; strong-coupling slope beta/4 at beta = 0.1; loop table equals single loops to 1e-12 and is identical for 1 and 7 threads).

GPU path (feature cuda; cuda/su2_update.cu + src/cuda.rs, C ABI, no crates): GpuLattice::from_cpu copies geometry (neighbour table), update classes, links and counters; sweep_with/update mirror the CPU, with the same Philox streams, staple order and quaternion formulas, compiled with -fmad=false. Independent tests in tests/cuda_compare.rs: over-relaxation bitwise equal to the CPU; heat bath agrees link by link with no accept decision differing and drift below 1e-9 over three updates.
Centre twists: optional plaquette_sign z_p = +-1 (Torus::plaquette_index), S = beta sum_p (1 - z_p a0(U_p)); the staple multiplies each term by the sign of its plaquette; action_density = mean z_p a0(U_p); set_twist(first, second) sets z_p = -1 on the (first, second) plaquettes at x_first = x_second = 0. Independent tests in tests/twist_2d.rs against character::torus_twist_2d; examples/twist_ratio_2d.rs estimates Z_tw/Z by thermodynamic integration over beta.
Update::Cool: U -> W^dagger/|W| (maximizes the local action term; deterministic), used by topology.rs.
Twist strength: twist_stack(first, second) lists the stack plaquettes; set_twist_strength(first, second, z) sets coupling z on the stack (set_twist = z -1); plaquette_sum(list). examples/twist_z integrates ln(Z_tw/Z) = -beta int_{-1}^{1} <sum_stack a0>_z dz (YM-N02 estimator); 2D validated against character::torus_twist_2d.
